# Kernel configuration fragment for a slim arm64 appliance image: what is
# particular to the architecture, on top of configs/slim-common.fragment
# beside this.
#
# Every symbol below was checked against a 6.18 arm64 kernel's own
# configuration, as in the common fragment -- and against what an arm64
# board is. This is one file for every board of the architecture, so what
# goes is what none of them has rather than what one of them lacks.
#
# What is deliberately left alone:
#
#  * every SoC's own ethernet MAC and the PHYs under it. A board is
#    reached over its network or it is not reached at all, and which MAC
#    it has is a property of the board rather than of the architecture.
#  * the SoC display drivers and simpledrm, and the AST and MGAG200 a
#    server's BMC gives it -- on some machines that is the only console.
#  * the SD/MMC, USB and PCIe host controllers boards boot from.
#  * what an arm64 virtual machine needs: virtio, 9p, and the serial
#    console the imager watches.
#
# It is deliberately shorter than the amd64 one. The rest of what an arm64
# image could drop is per board, and worth checking against a board that
# boots afterwards rather than guessing at here.

# Graphics cards of a desktop or a PC virtual machine, which no arm64
# board has. The SoC's own display driver and simpledrm are
# untouched, and so is the console a BMC provides.
# CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_RADEON is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_CIRRUS_QEMU is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_QXL is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_UDL is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_VMWGFX is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_XEN_FRONTEND is not set

# Ethernet cards of the PCI era. None of these is any SoC's MAC:
# every vendor that makes one is left enabled.
# CONFIG_NET_VENDOR_3COM is not set
# CONFIG_NET_VENDOR_8390 is not set
# CONFIG_NET_VENDOR_ADAPTEC is not set
# CONFIG_NET_VENDOR_AGERE is not set
# CONFIG_NET_VENDOR_ALACRITECH is not set
